{"author":"Michael Giver","author_email":"mikegiver@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"Progress 2026-07-29: Phase C committed as b411fb54 on giverm/OSCER-805-non-exclusion-orchestrator-wiring (unpushed, no PR yet). Built: trailing verification_data_source_check step + DataSourceCheckService; Determination::CALCULATION_TYPE_DATA_SOURCE_CE + CertificationCase#record_data_source_ce_determination for source-attested CE; negative determination relocated to the trailing step, routed via a new listener-less DeterminedCommunityEngagementNotMet; MockCommunityEngagement (order 20); runtime enforcement of declared_outcomes in Verification::DataSource#call.\n\nNaming deviation from the plan doc: the step is verification_data_source_check (not external_non_exclusion_check) and the service is DataSourceCheckService (not NonExclusionDeterminationService). 'External' in this codebase means data pushed INTO OSCER; this step is where OSCER calls OUT.\n\nAC deviations, both accepted: (1) the FEATURE_MOCK_DATA_SOURCES flag in the AC was dropped, superseded by PR #807's config-registration convention (already recorded 2026-07-28); (2) the AC says the CE check 'routes not-met members into the orchestrator' via existing events, but that had to become a NEW listener-less internal event. NotificationsEventListener binds handlers to event NAMES with no step awareness, so reusing a member-facing negative event would have emailed the member before sources were consulted, then a second contradictory email if a source excepted them.\n\nRUNTIME WALKTHROUGH FINDING (2026-07-29): drove the real cascade in dev and found MockCommunityEngagement could never fire in the shipped config, so the source-attested CE determination path had never executed end to end. mock_drug_treatment (PR #807) is consulted at the earlier exclusion step and terminates the case for 7 of 10 va_icn last digits (0/3/6/9 excluded; 1/5/7 excepted via was_in_drug_treatment), leaving only 2/4/8 to reach the orchestrator, all even, which is mock_emergency_county's branch under stop-on-first. No spec could catch it: each adapter spec asserts its own rule in isolation and each was correct, certification_business_process_spec stubs DataSourceCheckService outright, and the orchestrator's real-registry cases start from a Certification so they skip ExclusionDeterminationService. The failure existed only in the composition of two stages.\n\nFixed by re-keying MockCommunityEngagement off the member email (TRIGGER_EMAIL_SUBSTRING = 'ce-met', case-insensitive) rather than re-partitioning the va_icn keyspace. No determination path reads email (verified by grep), so the source is orthogonal to every va_icn-keyed source present or future; the substring idiom follows Auth::MockAdapter. Zero edits to already-merged mocks; order 20 unchanged. Added spec/business_processes/certification_business_process_reachability_spec.rb, which drives the real cascade with nothing in the determination path stubbed and asserts over the live registry that every enabled order-bearing source is creditable.\n\nVerification: full suite 3161 examples / 0 failures, 96.76% line and 84.24% branch, RuboCop clean across 573 files, and all 10 documented paths re-verified at runtime against the shipped config with exactly one determination each. Plan doc revised to as-built: Tech Specs/OSCER/non-exclusion-orchestrator-buildout-plan.md.\n\nRemaining: commit the fix, /review the branch, then push + open PR (base main, 'Part of #805')."},"env_id":"7fda8af9-5f39-45e1-9caf-59ffda62ec19","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785335900451852001,"uuid":"f357938e-9e65-411c-9052-f3bb8fe077f2"}